 "doc": "Mean and sample standard deviation (ddof 1) of every metric of stat.earth.seed1..8 (Earth, 1024x512, seeds 1 to 8). A port that draws its own random tables must land inside mean +- 3 std on every scalar metric and every component of the vectors (zonal, hist, coherence_by_lat, pole_std): params.n_sigma (zonal_lat is the band centers: exact, std 0). The Python mean and std themselves are held to the per-seed tolerances (means) and 5 % (std: 8 seeds estimate a std to about 25 %, so a port must not read it as tighter than that).",
